WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.610
- Today are going to talk
about what an average work week

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.050
looks like in the life
of a strategy consultant.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.870
Welcome to another coffee
break here on my channel

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.920
Firm Learning.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.250
My name is Heinrich on this
channel I want to help you

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.850
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.740
I worked as strategy consultant
for the consulting firm

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.910
McKinsey for about six years.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.640
And as you can imagine
I did lots of projects

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.870
throughout that time.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.980
Today, I'm talking about how
a typical work week look like

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.770
and I have to say that this is a work week

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.160
before the current health situation.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.450
So it reflects our typical
work week look like up until

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.470
about early this year and hopefully

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.450
how it will look like soon again.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.690
So to walk you through
a typical work week,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.260
I will now look down here on my screen

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.390
where I prepared a schedule for you.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.900
A work schedule for you
how this week looks like.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.330
Let's start with Monday.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.730
Monday is travel day.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:58.070
Usually you will fly in
from your office location

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.640
to the client on Monday.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.260
When exactly the flight goes depends a bit

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.210
on the flight schedule but
also your team preferences.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.043
I had studies.

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:09.080
I have projects where I needed
to take a 6:00 AM flight

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.240
in the morning on Monday

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.440
that of course is quite brutal
and can lead to you needing

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.940
to wake up at 4:00 AM every Monday.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.495
I would say average is getting
a flight around 7:00 AM

00:01:19.495 --> 00:01:22.310
7:30 AM but instead
those might require you

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.770
to stand up quite early
based on where you live.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.770
Then next, once you are at the client,

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.730
it is quite common to do
something like a check in

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.610
and check out every day with your team.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.810
So here are your team
lead we'll come together

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:36.960
with a whole team, sometimes all together,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.980
sometimes with everybody individually

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.400
and then talk to him what his
priorities are for the day

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.890
and then also at the checkout
at the end of the day,

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:48.150
what the associates
still have on their plate

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.920
also to help them
prioritize if he realizes

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.720
that maybe one guy really
has lots of stuff to do

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.520
which maybe isn't even required
on that specific evening.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.550
Then you will often have
a weekly client check-in.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.970
So you will sit together
with your main client,

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.800
with your main contact person.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.760
You will look into the
whole work week with firms,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.090
set the priorities for
the week, adjust the line

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.340
and do a quick check in with them.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.330
Afterwards, if you have some
time you will meet for lunch.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.640
So if the client has a nice canteen,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.170
you will often sit together
there with your team

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.100
and just have some lunch and
then after that frequently,

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.280
you will sit together and
interviews with clients.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.210
So these can be all kinds
of interview situations

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.690
says on the type of projects that you do.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.180
For instance, maybe a
finance guy from the client

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.140
sent you some data end of last week

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.710
and now you want to sit with them,

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.140
go over the data with them

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.840
and ask some clarifying
questions that you might have.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.160
Then you have a bit of
spare time where you sit

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.380
in the team room, to get some work done

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.490
and to do the checkout.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:46.620
Then after the checkout if
it's a bit of a more slow day

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.850
than often, you can then
jointly with the team,

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.850
drive to your hotel and you
might have a nice dinner

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.500
in the hotel restaurant
and then after dinner,

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.670
you go to your room and get some work done

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.420
from your hotel room and
here now in this example day,

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.850
you would be done at 10:00
PM with all your emails,

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:02.683
with everything.

00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:04.870
This is then where you can
really shut down your laptop

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.760
and being completely finished at 10:00 PM

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.580
is probably one of the better days.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.180
10:00 PM, we would have
considered it go day

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.350
if you're completely done
and finished on the day

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.150
and can really now watch a movie

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.420
or do something completely
odds after 10:00 PM.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.790
Then for the rest of the
week, you will often already

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.030
have some things locked
into your calendar.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.860
For instance, the daily
check-ins and check out,

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:29.320
this is something that you will
usually do every single day

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.500
and then on Thursday and on Friday,

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.980
you might do the checkout
a bit earlier on Thursday

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.950
to enable the team then to fly out

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:39.190
back to the office location and
on Friday to enable the team

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.750
to get out into the weekend
maybe slightly earlier.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.970
When exactly the check
in is so when you are

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:47.130
in the team room, this often
deviates a bit team by team.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.820
So usually what I've experienced
is that around 9:00 AM

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.970
is you do the check-in but
then people already come

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:54.400
into the team room
around 8:00 AM to 8:30 AM

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.040
to already get some first work done

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.150
and prepare the day a bit.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.420
Next you might also
have some internal calls

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.440
already scheduled.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.350
So one thing that you will
usually have once or twice

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.540
every week something called
a team problem solving

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.490
where you sit together
with the whole team.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.060
Often, also one of the
partners is flying in

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.300
joining you for the day,
sometimes also only by telephone

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.030
and where you then discuss
your progress with the partner.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.710
You discuss some challenges
that you are facing,

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.690
some things where you need his input on

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.330
and try to solve certain problems

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.600
that the client might be facing.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.860
Another thing that you were
frequently do are so called

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.520
internal expert calls so you
frequently look for experts

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.570
in your own consulting organization.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.750
So these are often more senior consultants

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.940
that have already worked
on a specific topic

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.730
several times in the past
and then you talk to them

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.670
and you try to get their input on,

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.320
what they are best practice is,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.460
what they believe how
your clients should solve

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:46.460
certain problems.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.010
Then you will also have some other

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.390
prescheduled client meetings.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.810
So frequently you have a weekly draw fixed

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.930
with the whole client team
where you sit together

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.180
with the whole team
discussing the progress

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.980
and then often every second week or so,

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.220
you have the steering committee
also called the Steerco.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.350
And this is usually the most
important meeting for you

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.290
in the week because this
is where you present

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.900
your project progress
to your project sponsor

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.130
on the client side and this
is often a board member.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.310
At least one board member present

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.000
sometimes even the whole board

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.050
or several board members present

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.270
and this is then really the
peak of the whole work week.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.930
The key deliverables where you
sit together with the clients

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.880
and you show them what your resides

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:30.670
are at this point in time.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.480
Well this being clear, then on Tuesday,

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.780
you come into the team
room, you have the check-in

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.350
and you conduct the Jour Fixe.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.670
For the Jour Fixe, you might
have prepared a document

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.140
last Monday night and
then after the Jour Fixe

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.030
maybe you just meet with another person

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.030
in the client organization
to just discuss some data

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.890
or some other questions
that you might have.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.710
Then you have the team problem solving

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.530
and here usually in such a week,

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.710
you're focused on the Steerco documents.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.220
Focus on the document
that you will present

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.860
to the Steerco on Thursday.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.400
And then frequently, now the partner

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.680
would have some suggestions,
some things he asks you

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.290
to implement in the document

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.220
and then he will ask you for a new meeting

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.800
on Wednesday afternoon
to discuss the things

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.090
that you're not asked to
do on the Steerco document.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.120
Then afterwards, what
we at least at McKinsey

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.390
always try to do something
called sports Tuesday

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.980
where you try just to block
some time for the whole team

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.970
to do some sports and often also

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.740
we did some group activities.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.080
You of course, what you do
depends a bit on your location,

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.710
what the possibilities are
so what we did for instance,

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.220
was renting a soccer place

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.230
where we were playing
some soccer as a team

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.280
or doing some CrossFit with a trainer

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.350
or just some team running,
just whatever the team fancied

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.680
and then after day like that,

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.150
everybody would just go
to his room frequently

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.770
and then just have dinner
for himself on the hotel room

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.100
and then just some last work

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.830
that everybody was doing for himself.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.460
Next Wednesday, the same drill
you get into the team room,

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.730
you do your check in
and then you might meet

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.450
with your key project
lead from the client side

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.330
because often then the
clients have a project leaders

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.420
where you forward the project
that you're working on

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.280
and often in the steering committees,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.610
you want actually the client
to present the documents

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:05.240
to not make it a consulting presentation

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.400
but rather presentation
that is really owned

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.010
by the client as well.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.040
This of course requires that you align

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.880
the whole presentation with the client

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.790
and who you often run into situations

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.930
where you actually you as
a team would like to put it

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.270
in a certain way but for whatever reason,

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.930
the client wants to have
things done a bit differently

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.370
so then you sit together with them,

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:26.360
you discuss and then you do
some changes on the document.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.210
Then you have the internal expert call

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.210
and then have some time
to get some more work done

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:33.110
before you talk to your
partner about the document.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.300
Unfortunately, what
frequently happens is that

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.450
maybe you as a team you
believe that document

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.220
is just perfect that
you're completely done

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.680
but then the partner looks at it

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:44.750
and now he tells to that he
has a completely different

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.720
opinion that actually wants to do it

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.120
the completely different way

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.283
and now you're really facing
situation that you actually

00:07:50.283 --> 00:07:53.400
need to send out the
document on that evening

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.890
so for the meeting next day

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.680
but now you suddenly realize that shoot,

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.647
you really have lots of stuff to do.

00:07:58.647 --> 00:08:01.170
And what you also maybe have
seen that maybe on Tuesday

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.670
and Wednesday, there wasn't enough time

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.610
to have a proper lunch.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.910
People might have just
done a quick working lunch

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.780
or even skipped lunch entirely
just to get the work done.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.530
So here is where because now you realize

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.500
that you have all the
stuff to do you just do

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.650
a very quick dinner in the team room

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.250
maybe you order some pizza
and then the whole team

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:20.320
sits together in a crunch
to really finish now

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.740
the Steerco doc based on
all the inputs that you got

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.140
both from your partner
but also from the client

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:27.330
in the morning and all
this can then easily

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:31.190
take you up until 1:00 AM at
night or sometimes even later.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.630
So this doesn't happen every
day but these days exist

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.800
and unfortunately, at
least from my experience,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.570
they exist a the bit more often

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:39.750
than you might have hoped for.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.300
And then next day even though
you're already stressed

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.970
and didn't have a lot of sleep,

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:46.870
at least I often try to prioritize sports.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.150
So for me, it was important
to always have at least

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.930
two units of sports during the work week.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.380
So what I would do often
try is then just put in

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.160
a little run at least in
the morning independent

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.800
of how long I worked last night okay.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.040
That was just my commitment
to keep me happy.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.450
But then later we would
go into the team room,

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.310
get some last work done, check-in

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.090
then the steering committee took place

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:08.920
and here then often other partners fly in,

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.150
the board members fly in
and for me it was always

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.450
an atmosphere a bit like
sitting in an exam, right.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:16.610
So you did all this study
and then the big meeting is

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.200
and then hopefully it
went really way far better

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.650
maybe even then you hope for

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:23.470
and then everybody is happy
and know that just imagine

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.180
that this is what happened here as well

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.800
then you maybe sit together, have lunch,

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.270
the partners there as well,
you can talk a bit with them

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:31.170
then you maybe have
another client discussion,

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.190
then some more work, then check out

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.750
and then you call it a day.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.610
So it was a good successful work week

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:38.920
because the Steerco went
well, everybody will be happy

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.380
and then you travel out.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:41.570
You fly out.

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:44.620
When exactly you fly out
also often a bit depends

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.140
just on the habits of the team

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.270
but of course also your
flight connections.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.180
So I'd say if I fly
out around five or six,

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.910
this would be rather early.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:56.120
If you fly out after eight,
this would be rather late.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:58.620
So something between
is what we usually had

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.670
and often frequently
you just book a flight,

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:03.360
you have it on standby because
you have flex tariffs.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.400
So you can all the time
reschedule your flight.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.890
Sometimes even after the
flight has already departed.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:08.837
So you will often just log into flight

00:10:08.837 --> 00:10:10.910
put in there for whatever reason

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:11.750
you need to take a later one

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.840
that you've just called your
travel team, you rescheduled it

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:14.920
and then just take a later one.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.080
Then Thursday evening at home you really,

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:19.510
there's not that much
stuff there is to do.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.080
Usually you then after you arrived,

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.780
maybe just write some emails
but then can call it a day.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.750
And then on Friday you either
work from your home office

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.470
or from the actual office.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.460
Here the culture might
differ a bit in between

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.670
the different MBB Firms, what is expected,

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:35.130
at least at McKinsey was
always completely fine

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:38.120
to pretty much always work from
the home office on Fridays.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.397
This is what you wanted to do.

00:10:39.397 --> 00:10:41.010
The only exception might've been,

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:43.280
if your project lead
came from the same office

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.870
where you are from that he
might ask yours to come in,

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.160
to sit with them on the
Friday in the office.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.760
Then Friday often was a little bit slower.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.730
You did some work but then
often you also had some time

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.870
to do admin tasks or participate

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:57.750
in any other office activities.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.230
So this can be grabbing a coffee

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:00.500
with someone other colleagues,

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.590
some other fun activities in the office

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.310
or often just doing your
expenses on a Friday.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.410
Then again, usually between five to six,

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.637
we had the checkout on Friday

00:11:08.637 --> 00:11:11.300
and then often you're able
ready to leave the office

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.240
at 6:00 PM and then call it a day

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.650
and then start into the weekend.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:15.920
Now regarding the weekend,

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:19.010
this was something I really
enjoyed in consulting

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.320
especially if you compare
it to investment banking

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.010
and this is that at least at McKinsey,

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:27.180
there was a very strong culture
that the weekend is free.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.660
You're really not expected to do any work

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.050
on the weekend at all.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:33.540
There might be some specific instances

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.730
where there's really a hard business need

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.510
where this is really
required and then yes,

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:39.190
you will be asked to work on the weekend

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.740
and this is all is expected from you

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.860
but this to me in my six years

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.550
really only happened a couple of times.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.210
Most of the times I was
really completely free

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.630
and didn't do anything.

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:51.500
What some people do like to
do is that then on Sunday

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.330
evening they take some
time prepare the week

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.040
but this was something
most cases I rather did

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.310
in the taxi Monday morning
or maybe even in the plane.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:03.050
So this isn't really required
if you don't wanna do that.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:03.890
So that's it guys.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.740
This is a typical work week.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:08.490
So probably just also to put
this a bit in perspective,

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.890
this is not one of the lighter weeks

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.560
but this is also not
one of the hardest weeks

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.600
that you can face, right.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.600
This is probably something in between

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.843
and usually the weeks
where you have Steercos

00:12:18.843 --> 00:12:21.010
or the Steerco weeks are a bit tougher

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.420
because you are into lots of pressure

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.580
of getting the document out and then off,

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:26.970
there are all these last
minute changes and inputs.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.930
So in this context, I would consider it

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.510
a representative week in MBB consulting.

